import json,re,sys
from pathlib import Path
root=Path(sys.argv[1]);data={}
CASES={
 'stale':('A reaction queued for the previous, larger cave',
  'The Borg updates on the second panel row of a large cave, queues the self-reaction of a trap detection, and then the level changes to a cave exactly one panel high - the height where the old-offset reset, which compares strictly, lets the old offsets through while the panel count yields a single row pair. The queued reaction still carries the old offsets and marks one row past the resized arrays: the original reads the row pointer one past the outer array and writes through it, and crashes.'),
 'fresh':('Control: a reaction queued for the current cave',
  'The same level change happens first, and the trap-detection reaction is queued afterwards, when the old offsets are the current ones. The next update processes it and marks the panel legitimately in both variants: the correction drops only reactions whose panel lies outside the current arrays.')}
for mode,(label,explanation) in CASES.items():
 item={'label':label,'explanation':explanation}
 for phase in ('before','after'):
  raw=(root/f'{phase}-{mode}.log').read_text()
  entry={'raw':raw,'passed':'native-c/detect-290 finished: 1/1 passed' in raw,
         'asan':'AddressSanitizer' in raw}
  for tag in ('GEOMETRY ','RATING ','OUTCOME '):
   match=re.search(re.escape(tag)+r'(.*)',raw)
   entry[tag.split()[0].lower()]=match[1].strip() if match else None
  item[phase]=entry
 data[mode]=item
html='''<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>The detection that outlived its cave</title><style>body{margin:0;background:#f4f1ea;color:#253a3c;font:18px/1.6 system-ui}main{max-width:1100px;margin:auto;padding:32px 24px}h1{font-size:40px;line-height:1.2}h2{font-size:24px}.cards{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:20px}.card{background:white;border:1px solid #cbd6d0;border-radius:12px;padding:24px;margin:18px 0}.cards .card{border-top:6px solid #648e80}.num{font-size:34px;font-weight:750}select,button{font:inherit;max-width:100%;padding:10px;border:1px solid #aabdb5;border-radius:7px;background:white}button{cursor:pointer;margin:14px 8px 0 0}button.active{background:#24685d;color:white}.summary{background:#e6eee6;padding:20px;border-left:5px solid #377367}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;overflow-wrap:anywhere;font:13px/1.5 monospace;max-height:330px;overflow:auto}details{background:white;padding:20px;margin:20px 0}summary{font-weight:700;cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:650px){.cards{grid-template-columns:1fr}h1{font-size:30px}}</style><main><p>Recorded native detection-reaction outcomes</p><h1>The detection that outlived its cave</h1><p>The Borg queues a self-reaction when it casts a detection spell, and processes it on the next update. A reaction queued before a level change keeps the old panel offsets, and its four-cell mark is indexed with them after the update resized the detection arrays for the new cave. On a new cave exactly one panel high - the height where the old-offset reset, which compares strictly, lets equal offsets through - the mark reads its row pointer one row past the arrays and writes through it. The supplied harness runs of this scenario segfaulted; the recorded native run does too.</p><section class="card"><label for="scenario">Choose a recorded situation</label><br><select id="scenario"></select><p id="explanation"></p><br><button data-step="0">Outcome</button></section><div class="cards"><section id="original" class="card"><h2>Original</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p></section><section id="compared" class="card"><h2>Corrected</h2><div class="num"></div><p class="state"></p></section></div><p class="summary" id="outcome"></p><h2>What the control establishes</h2><p>When the reaction is queued after the level change, with the current offsets, it marks the panel legitimately in both variants and the complete log is byte-identical: the correction drops only reactions whose panel lies outside the current arrays.</p><details><summary>Experiment conditions and limits</summary><p>Native Human Warrior level one, seed one thousand, a lit arena sized from the panel geometry of an eighty-by-thirty term (panel height twenty-eight): a large cave spanning several panel rows with the view pushed to the second row, then a cave exactly one panel high. The reaction is queued with the same call the spell casting path uses, the level change replaces the cave as the game does, and the scenario reads the resized arrays afterwards. The AddressSanitizer variant names the out-of-bounds row-pointer read in borg_handle_self; the plain variant records the crash. This isolates the queued-reaction bounds, not full autonomous play. No death or survival claim.</p></details><details><summary>Recorded native output</summary><h3>Original</h3><pre id="original-log"></pre><h3>Corrected</h3><pre id="compared-log"></pre></details><p>Canonical report: <a href="https://github.com/diegoami/neo-angband-tracker/issues/290">issue290</a>.</p></main><script>
const data=__DATA__;const select=document.getElementById('scenario');for(const [key,c] of Object.entries(data)){let o=document.createElement('option');o.value=key;o.textContent=c.label;select.append(o)}function draw(){let c=data[select.value];document.getElementById('explanation').textContent=c.explanation;for(const [panel,phase] of [['original','before'],['compared','after']]){let d=c[phase],p=document.getElementById(panel);p.querySelector('.num').textContent=d.passed?'Completed':(d.asan?'Sanitizer: out of bounds':'Crashed');p.querySelector('.state').textContent=d.geometry||'';document.getElementById(panel+'-log').textContent=d.raw}document.getElementById('outcome').textContent=select.value==='stale'?'The original crashes on the stale reaction (the sanitizer names the row-pointer read one past the arrays in borg_handle_self); the correction drops it and completes.':'The reaction belongs to the current cave: both variants mark the panel, byte for byte.';}select.addEventListener('change',draw);draw();</script></html>'''
(root/'replay.html').write_text(html.replace('__DATA__',json.dumps(data).replace('<','\\u003c')))
(root/'replay-data.json').write_text(json.dumps(data,indent=2)+'\n')
print('Open in your browser:',root/'replay.html')
